### C25D 1.0 test pattern: overlap_plates_100um_x_100um_li1_met1
### Modeled on klayout-pex's own test pattern
### testdata/designs/sky130A/test_patterns/overlap_plates_100um_x_100um_li1_m1.gds.gz
### (see https://github.com/iic-jku/klayout-pex/issues/184 for the real
### sky130A layer stack this is drawn from).
###
### Two 100um x 100um plates, fully overlapping in XY, on li1 and met1 -
### validates the zero-GROUND_PLANE / two-different-metal-layer code path
### in C25D2FasterCap.py (no ground-plane emulation needed here, unlike
### parallel_plate.c25d).
###
### Real li1/met1 Z heights from the C25D issue's own sky130A example:
###   li1:  Z_OFFSETS 0.9361 1.0111  (thickness 0.075um)
###   met1: Z_OFFSETS 1.3761 1.7361  (thickness 0.360um)
###   gap between li1 top and met1 bottom: 0.365um
###
### NOTE ON DIELECTRIC: the real sky130A stack in this gap uses
### DIELECTRIC_CONFORMAL (LINT) and DIELECTRIC_SIMPLE (NILD2) layers with
### varying permittivity (3.5-7.3) - not yet supported by
### C25D2FasterCap.py (see its module docstring). This fixture uses a
### single uniform DIELECTRIC_BACKGROUND (epsr=4.1, sky130A's base oxide
### value) as an approximation until that support is added. Do NOT treat
### any capacitance computed from this fixture as physically accurate for
### sky130A - it's a converter/geometry validation fixture, not a process
### model.
###
### NOTE ON SOLVER DIFFICULTY: 100um plates with only a 0.365um gap is an
### aspect ratio of ~274:1 - likely at least as hard for FasterCap to
### converge as parallel_plate_tight_margin.c25d's 25:1 case, possibly
### harder. If this doesn't converge cleanly, consider a variant with a
### smaller plate size before assuming there's a converter bug.

C25D 1.0
UNITS LENGTH um

META technology test_synthetic_based_on_sky130A
META source_cell overlap_plates_100um_x_100um_li1_met1

#---------------- LAYER (metal) ----------------
METAL li1  Z_OFFSETS 0.9361 1.0111
METAL met1 Z_OFFSETS 1.3761 1.7361

#---------------- DIELECTRICS ----------------
# Approximation only - see NOTE ON DIELECTRIC above.
DIELECTRIC_BACKGROUND diel PERMITTIVITY 4.100

#---------------- NETS and SHAPES ----------------
CONDUCTOR A A.net
BOX CONDUCTOR A LAYER li1 LL -50.000 -50.000 UR 50.000 50.000

CONDUCTOR B B.net
BOX CONDUCTOR B LAYER met1 LL -50.000 -50.000 UR 50.000 50.000

#---------------- DOMAIN ----------------
# XY margin generous relative to the 100um plates; Z margin modest
# relative to the ~0.8um total feature height (li1 bottom to met1 top).
DOMAIN_MARGIN X 20.000 Y 20.000 Z 2.000
